Chapter: BvtBadLoan
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-191: a save refusing the economy for its loans names the first bad loan and its fields (ev-bad-loan). Answers a
 bit per check: 1 a new economy names no bad loan, 2 an open loan whose due hour has passed is named with its id, due,
 status and hour, 4 that loan's slot read clean again once it defaults (status 3); -9 is a fixture that did not build.
 7 is all.
  bbl-run : Integer -> Integer
  bbl-run (unused) = when bb-economy 0
    is Err (_) -> -9
    is Ok (x) -> let m = x.world.money
      in let clean = if ev-bad-loan m 0 == "" & ev-loans m 0 then 1 else 0
      in let l = list-at m.loans 0
      in let a = __record-set l "lender" 1
      in let b = __record-set l "borrower" 2
      in let c = __record-set l "principal" 10
      in let d = __record-set l "due" (m.hour + 1)
      in let e = __record-set l "status" 1
      in let f = __record-set m "loan-count" 1
      in let g = __record-set m "hour" (m.hour + 1)
      in let said = ev-bad-loan m 0
      in let named = if not (ev-loans m 0) & text-starts-with said " id=1 " & text-contains said (" due=" & show l.due & " paid=0 status=1 hour=" & show m.hour) then 2 else 0
      in let h = __record-set l "status" 3
      in let healed = if ev-loans m 0 & ev-bad-loan m 0 == "" then 4 else 0
      in if m.purse-count < 2 then -8 else clean + named + healed
  bvt-bad-loan : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-bad-loan (unused) = act
    n <- bbl-run 0
    a <- bvt-check ("a save refusing the loans names the first bad loan and its fields (UOAIX-191, code " & show n & ")") (n == 7)
    a
  end
